    summary: 'A GEMM kernel computes `C = α·A·B + β·C` by assigning each thread block an output tile, streaming K in chunks through shared memory and issuing tensor-core instructions on fragments held in registers. Its performance depends on tile shape, pipeline depth, how many tiles the grid produces relative to the SM count, and above all on arithmetic intensity: prefill GEMMs with thousands of tokens are compute-bound, decode GEMMs with a handful of rows are bound by streaming the weights from HBM.',
